# Trivy baseline for the eg-esign container image (jenkins/build-image.groovy).
# Reviewed 2026-07-27.
#
# Separate from .trivyignore on purpose. That file covers the source tree; this
# one additionally covers CVEs that live in the base image and build toolchain,
# which no change to package.json can resolve. Keeping them apart stops
# image-only exceptions from silently weakening the dependency scan.
#
# Anything not listed here still fails the build and blocks the deploy.
# Re-triage whenever the node base image is bumped.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same app-level findings baselined in .trivyignore (Trivy takes one ignorefile,
# so this file has to be a superset). See .trivyignore for the full reasoning.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2   # react-router 7 -> 8, a framework major
CVE-2026-45623        # postcss nested under next
GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849   # postcss nested under next
CVE-2026-14257        # brace-expansion nested in build-time packages
GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj   # sharp; 0.35.0 breaks the build (TS7016)

# brace-expansion 2.0.2 (DoS, exponential-time expansion). Image-only: the
# source lockfile resolves nested copies to 2.1.2, but the image is built from
# `turbo prune` output, which re-resolves and keeps a 2.0.2. The root copy is
# overridden to 5.0.8 either way. Verified present by scanning the built image
# rather than inferred from the lockfile.
CVE-2026-13149

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# npm's own bundled dependencies, from the node:22-alpine3.22 base image.
# Not reachable from package.json — they ship inside
# /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm. Bumping the base does not fix them: the
# CRITICAL tar needs 7.5.19 and even node:24-alpine ships 7.5.15. npm cannot
# simply be removed either — docker/start.sh runs `npx prisma migrate deploy`
# on every boot.
#
# Reachability: npm's tar is used to unpack registry tarballs. The runtime
# container never installs packages; it runs one prisma migration against an
# already-installed dependency tree, so there is no untrusted archive to parse.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-59873        # tar 7.5.11 (CRITICAL) -> 7.5.19
CVE-2026-59874        # tar 7.5.11 -> 7.5.18
CVE-2026-48815        # sigstore 3.1.0 -> 4.1.1 (npm's provenance verifier)
CVE-2026-33671        # picomatch 4.0.3 -> 4.0.4

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go stdlib compiled into the esbuild binary at
# packages/email/node_modules/@esbuild/linux-x64/bin/esbuild.
#
# esbuild arrives transitively: upstream Documenso declares `react-email` (a
# CLI/preview tool) as a production dependency of packages/email, so
# `npm ci --only=production` keeps it. Only @react-email/render is used at
# runtime; the esbuild binary is never executed by the running service.
# Moving react-email to devDependencies would remove these outright, but it
# edits upstream packaging and would be re-fought by the nightly
# upstream-sync merges — tracked separately rather than patched here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
